<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35974" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνόρνῡμι</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνῶρσα</span>: 
			Ep.
		
		aor. 2
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνῶρτο</span>:—the only two tenses
		used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>arouse, stir
				up in</i> a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇσιν γόον ἐνῶρσεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.499
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιοῖς] ἀνάλκιδα φύζαν ἐνόρσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.62
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δὲ σθένος ὦρσεν ἑκάστῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.451
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόβον τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.544
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχαν</span>] (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμμιν</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				23.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος δ᾽ ἐνῶρσε . . στρατῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					713
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>arise in</i> or <i>among,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνῶρτο γέλως θεοῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.599
				</span></i>
			.</div>
